The system may override your age gates based on the local regulations of the person's geographic location.
Age ranges provide the minimum information necessary for content decisions while protecting privacy.
Parental controls and family sharing settings may affect the availability and accuracy of age information.

members.comment:
Returns a response indicating whether the person shared their age range.

Regional requirements may override your age gates based on the person's location.

Use <doc://com.apple.documentation/documentation/swiftui/environmentvalues/requestagerange> with SwiftUI environment values to request age ranges in response to user interactions:

```swift
struct ContentView: View {
    @Environment(\.requestAgeRange) var requestAgeRange

    var body: some View {
        Button("Check Age Range") {
            Task {
                do {
                    let response = try await requestAgeRange(ageGates: 13, 16, 18)
                    switch response {
                    case let .sharing(ageRange):
                        // Person shared their age range.
                        break
.                    case .declinedSharing:
                        // In regulated regions, the system automatically provides the person's age range — the person can't decline sharing.
                        break
                    }
                } catch {
                    // Handle error.
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
```

- Parameters:
  - threshold1: The primary age threshold for your app.
  - threshold2: An optional second age threshold that creates an additional age range.
  - threshold3: An optional third age threshold that creates a final age range.
- Returns: A response indicating whether the person declared their age range. If the person shared their
age range, the system also returns the age range.
- Throws: An error if the request fails.

declarations.comment:
An action that presents a system interface for significant app update acknowledgments.

Use this action to inform people about important changes to your app that require their acknowledgment before proceeding.

```swift
struct ContentView: View {
    @Environment(\.showSignificantUpdateAcknowledgment) var showSignificantUpdate

    var body: some View {
        Button("Review Update") {
            Task {
                do {
                    try await showSignificantUpdate(updateDescription: "We've updated our privacy policy.")
                } catch {
                    // Handle error.
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
```

members.comment:
Presents a system interface to request acknowledgment of significant app changes from people, or their parents or guardians.

Call this method when you make significant changes to your app that require acknowledgment before people continue using it.

```swift
struct ContentView: View {
    @Environment(\.showSignificantUpdateAcknowledgment) var showSignificantUpdate

    var body: some View {
        Button("Review Update") {
            Task {
                do {
                    try await showSignificantUpdate(updateDescription: "We've updated our privacy policy.")
                } catch {
                    // Handle error.
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
```

- Parameter updateDescription: A clear description of what changed in your app and why acknowledgment is required.
- Throws: An error if the feature isn't available.
